/*
  interface/sender.spthy -- INTERFACE LAYER (orange #f2994a), Alex's pane, V3 layered template.
  One rule per control. The interface PROMPTS the user (!Step + !StepData observables), the stressor
  layer reads those prompts, and the human's mask answers; a *_go / adapter turns the answer into a
  protocol fact. No rule here touches the wire or the crypto (those are protocol/kdf.spthy).

  Steps posed:
    calc_sk  (compute, UNDER DEADLINE)  -- derive SK = kdf(N_A,N_B); !StepData carries the correct
                            value the step should yield. The compute masks (core/masks/compute_behavior)
                            answer: Attentive -> correct, Busy -> slip (fresh wrong key), Careless ->
                            timeout. The control is presented UNDER A TIMER (the session-establishment
                            deadline -- the handshake must complete before the peer gives up), so it
                            emits !UnderDeadline(rid): sigma3 time_pressure_deadline reads that context,
                            never a task name. (Dangles harmlessly where sigma3-deadline is absent.)
  (Post-KDF controls -- approve / verify / authorize / set-policy -- are added by the profiles that
   exercise them, each as one more interface rule reading !Session; see interface/postkdf.spthy.)
*/

rule IF_calc_alex [color=#f2994a]:
    [ AlexHasNonces(idA, <Na, Nb>), Fr(~rid) ]
  --[ UIStep('Alex', 'calc_sk') ]->
    [ !Step('Alex', ~rid, 'compute'),
      !StepData('Alex', ~rid, kdf(Na, Nb)),
      !UnderDeadline(~rid),
      AlexAwaitKey(idA, ~rid) ]
